message: "If you use cpmdc, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cpmdc: a C ABI for embedding OpenCPMD with Cap'n Proto parameters"
authors:
  - family-names: Goswami
    given-names: Rohit
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2393-8056"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmniPotentRPC/cpmdc"
url: "https://cpmdc.rgoswami.me"
# [[[cog cog.outl(f'version: "{open("version.txt").read().strip()}"') ]]]
version: "0.4.0"
# [[[end]]]
license: MIT
keywords:
  - CPMD
  - OpenCPMD
  - Car-Parrinello
  - density functional theory
  - Cap'n Proto
  - C ABI
abstract: >-
  The C application binary interface (ABI) layer for embedding OpenCPMD in
  OmniPotentRPC tools.
  It gives non-Fortran callers one stable boundary for CPMD setup,
  geometry steps, feature discovery, and result messages, with method
  setup passed as a serialized Cap'n Proto CPMDParams message and each
  geometry step as a ForceInput message.
